        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 63,
          "text": "1. Purpose"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 87,
          "text": "This policy establishes the principles, criteria, and controls governing the recognition and measurement of Order"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 102,
          "text": "Intake across the Company. This version supersedes v1.0 and introduces enhanced controls following the 2024"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 114,
          "text": "internal audit cycle."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 144,
          "text": "2. Scope"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 168,
          "text": "This policy applies to all business units, regions, and legal entities that generate, process, or record customer orders"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 183,
          "text": "under the Order-to-Cash (O2C) cycle, including:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 201,
          "text": "- Hardware and Software arrangements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 219,
          "text": "- Standalone Services arrangements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 237,
          "text": "- Bundled multi-element arrangements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 267,
          "text": "3. Definitions"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 294,
          "text": "3.1 Order"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 315,
          "text": "A binding agreement between the Company and a customer, evidenced by BOTH a Purchase Order AND a"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 330,
          "text": "countersigned contract (see 5.2)."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 354,
          "text": "3.2 Order Backlog"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 372,
          "text": "The cumulative value of Orders recognized as Order Intake but not yet delivered, fulfilled, or recognized as revenue."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 402,
          "text": "4. Roles and Responsibilities"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "table",
          "top": 425.0,
          "rows": [
            [
              "Role",
              "Responsibility"
            ],
            [
              "Sales Operations",
              "Order capture; ensures PO + contract obtained"
            ],
            [
              "Finance Business Partners",
              "Recognition criteria review"
            ],
            [
              "Regional Finance Head",
              "Risk sign-off (elevated from v1.0)"
            ],
            [
              "Group Treasury",
              "Publishes month-end FX spot rates"
            ],
            [
              "Group Finance (Revenue Assurance)",
              "Policy ownership and testing"
            ]
          ],
          "n_rows": 6,
          "n_cols": 2
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 561,
          "text": "5. Order Intake Recognition and Measurement"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 588,
          "text": "5.1 Recognition Criteria for Order Intake"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 609,
          "text": "An order shall be recognized as Order Intake when ALL of the following conditions are met:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 630,
          "text": "- A legally binding contract or Purchase Order (PO) exists, AND"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 648,
          "text": "- The order value can be reliably measured, AND"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 663,
          "text": "- Collectability is reasonably assured (see 5.3)."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 687,
          "text": "KEY CHANGE FROM v1.0"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 711,
          "text": "Collectability is now a recognition precondition, not merely a downstream approval trigger."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 750,
          "text": "CFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | CONTROLLED DOCUMENT Page 2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_number": 3,
      "extraction_method": "text",
      "char_count": 1603,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 63,
          "text": "5.2 Customer Commitment"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 84,
          "text": "Customer commitment must be evidenced by BOTH:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 102,
          "text": "- A signed Purchase Order"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 120,
          "text": "- A countersigned contract"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 135,
          "text": "Orders supported by a PO alone do NOT qualify for recognition."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 159,
          "text": "5.3 Collectability Assessment"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 186,
          "text": "5.3.1 Risk Scoring Model"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 207,
          "text": "Collectability is assessed using a combined weighted risk score:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 225,
          "text": "Risk Score = (0.40 × Credit Rating Score) + (0.35 × Payment History Score) + (0.25 × Country Risk Score)"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 246,
          "text": "Each component is scored on a 0–100 scale. Credit Rating Score is derived from Group Credit Risk classification;"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 258,
          "text": "Payment History Score is based on trailing 12-month payment behavior; Country Risk Score is published quarterly by"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 273,
          "text": "Group Treasury."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "table",
          "top": 289.5,
          "rows": [
            [
              "Risk Score Range",
              "Classification",
              "Action Required"
            ],
            [
              "80–100",
              "Low Risk",
              "None"
            ],
            [
              "50–79",
              "Medium Risk",
              "Standard booking"
            ],
            [
              "Below 50",
              "High Risk",
              "Regional Finance Head review"
            ]
          ],
          "n_rows": 4,
          "n_cols": 3
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 381,
          "text": "5.3.2 Escalation Requirements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 402,
          "text": "Orders scoring below 50 require MANDATORY Regional Finance Head sign-off prior to booking."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 426,
          "text": "5.4 Timing for Booking of Order Intake"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 447,
          "text": "Order Intake shall be booked ONLY once BOTH of the following are received and verified by Finance:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 468,
          "text": "- Signed Purchase Order"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 483,
          "text": "- Countersigned contract"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 510,
          "text": "5.5 Orders in Non-Euro Currencies"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 537,
          "text": "5.5.1 Conversion Methodology"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 555,
          "text": "Converted Order Value (EUR) = Order Value (Local Currency) ÷ Month-End Spot Rate"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 576,
          "text": "The Month-End Spot Rate is published by Group Treasury as of the booking date."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 600,
          "text": "5.5.2 FX Variance Control"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 618,
          "text": "-"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 621,
          "text": "FX Variance (%) = |Booking Rate Order Date Rate| ÷ Order Date Rate × 100"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 639,
          "text": "If FX Variance (%) > 5%, the order must be:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 660,
          "text": "- Flagged in the system"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 678,
          "text": "- Routed to the Controller for review prior to final booking"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 708,
          "text": "6. Order Intake Approvals"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 750,
          "text": "CFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | CONTROLLED DOCUMENT Page 3"
        }
      ]
    },
